{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1453953-v20-choosing","id":1453953,"title":"V20 - choosing","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-07-01T10:53:19-07:00","id":1453953,"title":"V20 - choosing","content":"Greetings all, I have a question:<br /> <br /> If you had to choose would you go for elder powers of Protean or of Auspex and which ones would you take?<br /> At the moment I would lean towards auspex over Protean since more uses and more versatile (telepathic communication seems incredibly potent just like Clairvoyance...) but things like skin of marble can save your unlife quite easily.<br /> <br /> So what would you guys go for? What seems the best choice and why?<br /> For arguments sake imagine you could somehow go all the way up to level 9.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26925-denstoffy","name":"Denstoffy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26925_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-01T12:26:40-07:00","id":1453960,"title":"","content":"Ehh... It should really depend on the character you're playing/making. It's hard to pick which one is &quot;best&quot; if you don't know the type of character, the type of game, the type of role or anything else.<br /> <br /> What are you aiming to do with your elder?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-01T13:35:22-07:00","id":1453962,"title":"","content":"Elder-level Protean allows a vampire to react to hazardous situations, avoid damage, and escape with their unlife. Elder-level Auspex allows a vampire to be aware of potentially-hazardous situations to begin with, and avoid or preempt them. Given a choice between the two, I'd take Auspex first every time.<br /> <br /> Hell, in my TC game I pretty much told my players outright that Auspex is pretty much the &quot;great filter&quot; for whether a vampire survives to their elder years or not, and vampires without Auspex need a <i>damned</i> compelling combination of disciplines and mental acuity to compensate -- and even then, they're likely at a severe disadvantage. They're at the point Assamites start running buck wild through eastern Europe, so they're about a story or two from learning that the hard way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 07-01-2021, 04:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-01T14:49:37-07:00","id":1453970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1453953-v20-choosing?p=1453962#post1453962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Elder-level Protean allows a vampire to react to hazardous situations, avoid damage, and escape with their unlife. Elder-level Auspex allows a vampire to be aware of potentially-hazardous situations to begin with, and avoid or preempt them. Given a choice between the two, I'd take Auspex first every time.<br /> <br /> Hell, in my TC game I pretty much told my players outright that Auspex is pretty much the &quot;great filter&quot; for whether a vampire survives to their elder years or not, and vampires without Auspex need a <i>damned</i> compelling combination of disciplines and mental acuity to compensate -- and even then, they're likely at a severe disadvantage. They're at the point Assamites start running buck wild through eastern Europe, so they're about a story or two from learning that the hard way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I've had similar thoughts. Really, the Toreador are the best equipped for surviving in the modern world. In the age of bombs and snipers, the best Disciplines are those that let you know someone is about to attempt to assassinate you, to run away immediately, and control any groups of humans who might aid you or your assassin, or conduct mundane investigations into why the attack happened in the first place. The Torries have that on lock. The Malks and Tremere are up there as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-01T14:58:25-07:00","id":1453973,"title":"","content":"Honestly? C) buy a number of other disciplines up to 5 instead of buying one up to 9 because more general tools will be handy more often than the often specialized abilities of elder disciplines.<br /> <br /> When all you have is a hammer in your single uber discipline you\u2019ll always be looking for ways to make problems into nails. A Nosferatu with Potence 9 isn\u2019t going to be looking too hard for solutions that don\u2019t involve brute strength. One with Animalism 5, Obfuscate 5 and Potence 5 (which is basically the same XP cost) has way more tools and approaches to solving their problems.<br /> <br /> Now, to be fair, Protean and Auspex are both far more flexible than Potence, but the general point remains; flexibility is a power unto itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-01T20:57:20-07:00","id":1454049,"title":"","content":"I <b>have</b> taken elder discipline powers in Protean, but for a specific character whose concept required more dots devoted to shapeshifting than any other discipline. Even so, I probably got at least as much utility out of 3 dots in Dominate as twice that many in Protean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-02T07:40:31-07:00","id":1454078,"title":"","content":"Elder auspex is pretty bad in my opinion.The only exception is Psychic Assault but it's only worth it if your character has a VERY large pool of dice to roll, something like 14 dice, and Precognition. Karmic Vision is fun, but requires too much luck in the dice. So there's that. Instead of elder auspex, use GPS, google maps, <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">ear piece and drones.<br /> <br /> Protean however is another tale.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> Shape Mastery (6) was good in Revised but trash in v20, so it only worth if you can convince your st to use the Revised version instead of the v20 one. Spectral Body, Inward Focus and Loki's Gift are all good. Note that you can create you own power too, so maybe try an phoenix form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-02T19:37:32-07:00","id":1454109,"title":"","content":"Interesting that you pick those two. I think Earth Control and Telepathic Communication are both great, T.C. is great a lot, E.C. is amazing when you need it. I don't like Spectral Body, it's over powered and I wouldn't like a player to have it for it's potential to annoy me as a story teller. Inward focus is just plain broken if that's the one that multiplies with Celerity, never would I allow it. Loki's gift is a great level 6 ability. I find the elder stuff if left unchecked fun breaking a lot of the time because the balance is just not there and then you can do things that negate the need to roleplay and figure things out more and more.<br /> <br /> The problem to watch out for when running elder games is some players will make truly broken characters while others because they are not as well versed or more about flavor will end up sooo behind in power that the games become very difficult to run. I could not make a game of fourth gens work for this reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24221,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","user":"Vamps Like Us","date":". 07-02-2021, 10:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-02T20:02:56-07:00","id":1454112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blailton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1453953-v20-choosing?p=1454078#post1454078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Instead of elder auspex, use GPS, google maps, ear piece and drones.</div> </div> </div> </div>And be vulnerable to hacking, counter-surveillance, and electronic countermeasures -- none of which work against Auspex, and are fairly commonplace in a contemporary setting. And, it's something elders typically aren't known for, which is something of a given when discussing elder-level powers. That's what childer are for.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, you're selling Auspex dramatically short. Clairvoyance is extremely handy, and has the side benefit that your targets won't be aware they're being spied upon. Prediction is an &quot;I win&quot; button for social scenes. Cipher's either incredibly overpowered or completely useless, depending upon what type of chronicle the ST is running.<br /> <br /> Anima Gathering is just stupidly overpowered if the character has a coterie or pawns capable of using astral projection to full effect. Mirror Reflex used to be to defense what Flower of Death was offense, and got correspondingly (over-)nerfed in V20 -- and honestly still isn't too shabby, especially in the hands of a character with Celerity which can play the action economy game. Omniscience is exactly what it says on the tin, and let's not forget the ludicrous grand-daddy of discipline powers -- False Slumber.<br /> <br /> Nothing like being completely active while in torpor, able to influence anything basically anywhere at any time, and probably<i> more</i> powerful for it because the vampire isn't inhibited having to haul a dessicated, vulnerable, meat sack around. One could make their case still having the silver string is a hell of a drawback, but we're talking about fourth generation methuselahs...good luck cutting it unless you're a vampire of equal or greater power in the astral plane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-03T04:28:48-07:00","id":1454122,"title":"","content":"Thank you everybody for the feedback that was already provided.<br /> <br /> We are indeed playing an elder game with a very limited amount of players and hence we were able to get an extra clan discipline (for 5 freebies) which for me, playing a gangrel, was Auspex.<br /> Hence why the comparison between auspex and protean since I don't really see any great potential in animalism ( but that could be me...) and fortitude isn't going to drastically rock the boat.<br /> <br /> Since we are two, I'm playing (we are in anci\u00ebnt Mesopotamia) the ruler of a city state and as far as I remember, a very atypical gangrel since I have skills like commerce and politics etc and am heavy into backgrounds (you have to kinda run the place...) but I am not a slouch in combat at all (some celerity/potence was picked up). The other player is going to combat/spymaster/underhand route and is an absolute terror in close combat.<br /> <br /> There are very few to no vampires around to learn disciplines from and you need them to learn anything which isn't in-clan or a physical discipline so I was kinda weighing my options.<br /> At the moment I'm favoring auspex for the use as a ruler and going for telepathic communication (directing from afar sounds incredibly powerful) as well as clairvoyance (to keep appraised of what is happening at different locations.)<br /> <br /> I would love to pick up some other disciplines but as stated, it's kinda hard with very few to no vampires around at this time and age...<br /> So GPS, google maps etc are all atm not an option. I think we are at this point in time 1000 years from the first script being developped so that won't be an option for the next few milennia.<br /> <br /> The campaign is slow building with choices affecting how things are going and the world evolves which suits us fine. <br /> If there are any disciplines or ideas you guy wish to share which could help us, that would be wonderful.<br /> <br /> Presence seems like something I'd want a lot, same for dominate since that would out the social kit very nicely <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And at elder level, they both seem very powerful and easy to combine with what I already got.<br /> <br /> If anybody got great ideas for animalism, which atm is the discipline I'm neglecting a lot, please feel free to share them. It might be good to hear it's not a total loss. Atm I have it at 2.<br /> <br /> Again, thank you for all the feedback and keep the ideas comming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26925-denstoffy","name":"Denstoffy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26925_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}